{"primaryContentSections":[{"kind":"content","content":[{"type":"heading","level":2,"anchor":"Overview","text":"Overview"},{"type":"paragraph","inlineContent":[{"isActive":true,"type":"reference","identifier":"doc:\/\/Swidux\/documentation\/Swidux\/UndoPlugin"},{"type":"text","text":" captures state snapshots before each undoable action. Undo history lives in memory (lost on relaunch), but restored state is persisted normally via "},{"isActive":true,"type":"reference","identifier":"doc:\/\/Swidux\/documentation\/Swidux\/EntityStore"},{"type":"text","text":"’s "},{"code":"restore(from:)","type":"codeVoice"},{"type":"text","text":"."}]},{"type":"paragraph","inlineContent":[{"type":"text","text":"If you don’t use "},{"isActive":true,"type":"reference","identifier":"doc:\/\/Swidux\/documentation\/Swidux\/UndoPlugin"},{"type":"text","text":", nothing changes. It’s fully opt-in."}]},{"type":"heading","level":2,"anchor":"Adding-Undo-to-Your-App","text":"Adding Undo to Your App"},{"type":"heading","level":3,"anchor":"1-Create-the-plugin","text":"1. Create the plugin"},{"inlineContent":[{"type":"text","text":"Pass declarative predicates to classify which actions are undoable and which coalesce:"}],"type":"paragraph"},{"code":["let isUndoable: @Sendable (AppAction) -> Bool = { action in","    switch action {","    case .items(.create), .items(.delete), .items(.rename): true","    case .selectItem, .toggleSidebar: false","    }","}","","let undoPlugin = UndoPlugin<AppState, AppAction>(","    isUndoable: isUndoable,","    coalescing: { action in","        if case .items(.rename) = action { return true }","        return false","    }",")"],"type":"codeListing","syntax":"swift"},{"anchor":"2-Register-and-pass-to-Store","text":"2. Register and pass to Store","type":"heading","level":3},{"inlineContent":[{"type":"text","text":"Register the plugin with "},{"identifier":"doc:\/\/Swidux\/documentation\/Swidux\/PluginHost","type":"reference","isActive":true},{"type":"text","text":" for lifecycle hooks, and pass it directly to "},{"isActive":true,"type":"reference","identifier":"doc:\/\/Swidux\/documentation\/Swidux\/Store"},{"type":"text","text":" for undo\/redo methods and "},{"code":"canUndo","type":"codeVoice"},{"type":"text","text":"\/"},{"code":"canRedo","type":"codeVoice"},{"type":"text","text":" tracking:"}],"type":"paragraph"},{"code":["let plugins = PluginHost<AppState, AppAction>()","plugins.register(undoPlugin)","plugins.register(persistencePlugin)","","return Store(","    initialState: AppState(),","    reducer: { state, action in","        reducer.reduce(state: &state, action: action, environment: environment)","    },","    plugins: plugins,","    undoPlugin: undoPlugin,","    persistencePlugin: persistencePlugin,","    isUndoable: isUndoable",")"],"type":"codeListing","syntax":"swift"},{"inlineContent":[{"code":"Store","type":"codeVoice"},{"type":"text","text":" handles the rest internally: snapshotting state before undoable actions, restoring via "},{"code":"applyRestore","type":"codeVoice"},{"type":"text","text":" on undo\/redo, draining persistence changes, and updating "},{"type":"codeVoice","code":"canUndo"},{"type":"text","text":"\/"},{"type":"codeVoice","code":"canRedo"},{"type":"text","text":"."}],"type":"paragraph"},{"type":"heading","level":3,"text":"3. Wire platform UI","anchor":"3-Wire-platform-UI"},{"type":"paragraph","inlineContent":[{"type":"strong","inlineContent":[{"type":"text","text":"macOS"}]},{"type":"text","text":" — replace the Edit menu:"}]},{"code":["WindowGroup { ... }",".commands {","    CommandGroup(replacing: .undoRedo) {","        Button(\"Undo\") { store.undo() }","            .keyboardShortcut(\"z\", modifiers: .command)","            .disabled(!store.canUndo)","        Button(\"Redo\") { store.redo() }","            .keyboardShortcut(\"z\", modifiers: [.command, .shift])","            .disabled(!store.canRedo)","    }","}"],"syntax":"swift","type":"codeListing"},{"type":"paragraph","inlineContent":[{"inlineContent":[{"type":"text","text":"iOS"}],"type":"strong"},{"type":"text","text":" — bridge the system UndoManager for shake-to-undo:"}]},{"type":"codeListing","syntax":"swift","code":["\/\/ In your view — connect the environment UndoManager:",".onAppear { store.undoManager = undoManager }",".onChange(of: undoManager) { _, new in store.undoManager = new }"]},{"type":"paragraph","inlineContent":[{"code":"Store","type":"codeVoice"},{"type":"text","text":" automatically registers undo\/redo actions with the "},{"code":"UndoManager","type":"codeVoice"},{"type":"text","text":" after each undoable dispatch."}]},{"level":2,"anchor":"Coalescing","text":"Coalescing","type":"heading"},{"type":"paragraph","inlineContent":[{"type":"text","text":"The "},{"type":"codeVoice","code":"coalescing"},{"type":"text","text":" predicate groups consecutive matching actions into a single undo step. The first coalescing action captures a snapshot; subsequent consecutive coalescing actions share that snapshot. A non-coalescing action or undo\/redo resets the flag. Typing “hello” produces one undo entry, not five."}]},{"type":"heading","level":2,"anchor":"Undo-and-sync","text":"Undo and sync"},{"type":"paragraph","inlineContent":[{"type":"text","text":"Undo is scoped to changes the local user made. If another device deletes an entity and the merge surfaces that mid-session, "},{"type":"codeVoice","code":"restore(from:)"},{"type":"text","text":" will not bring the row back, even though older undo snapshots still contain it."}]},{"inlineContent":[{"type":"text","text":"That has to be the rule, because the alternative is worse than a missing undo step: restoring the row records it as a "},{"inlineContent":[{"type":"text","text":"creation"}],"type":"strong"},{"type":"text","text":", which syncs out and re-seeds every peer that had already agreed it was gone. One person’s undo would undo everybody’s delete."}],"type":"paragraph"},{"inlineContent":[{"isActive":true,"type":"reference","identifier":"doc:\/\/Swidux\/documentation\/Swidux\/EntityStore"},{"type":"text","text":" tracks this in "},{"code":"remotelyRemovedIDs","type":"codeVoice"},{"type":"text","text":". An ID leaves the set the moment it becomes local again — the user creates it, or the row reappears on disk because the other device undid "},{"inlineContent":[{"type":"text","text":"its"}],"type":"emphasis"},{"type":"text","text":" delete — so nothing is permanently un-undoable. See "},{"type":"reference","isActive":true,"identifier":"doc:\/\/Swidux\/documentation\/Swidux\/EntityStoreGuide"},{"type":"text","text":" for the mechanics."}],"type":"paragraph"},{"inlineContent":[{"type":"text","text":"Apps that don’t sync never hit this: nothing populates the set, and undo behaves exactly as it always has."}],"type":"paragraph"},{"anchor":"Memory","text":"Memory","type":"heading","level":2},{"inlineContent":[{"type":"text","text":"Each snapshot is a value-type copy of your state. Cost is proportional to the number of entities across all stores. Use "},{"code":"maxDepth","type":"codeVoice"},{"type":"text","text":" to bound memory for large state:"}],"type":"paragraph"},{"syntax":"swift","code":["let undoPlugin = UndoPlugin<AppState, AppAction>(maxDepth: 50, ...)"],"type":"codeListing"}]}],"schemaVersion":{"minor":3,"major":0,"patch":0},"seeAlsoSections":[{"anchor":"Reference","identifiers":["doc:\/\/Swidux\/documentation\/Swidux\/MacrosReference","doc:\/\/Swidux\/documentation\/Swidux\/PluginKillswitchReference","doc:\/\/Swidux\/documentation\/Swidux\/PluginParentalGateReference","doc:\/\/Swidux\/documentation\/Swidux\/PluginPaywallReference","doc:\/\/Swidux\/documentation\/Swidux\/PluginAnalyticsReference","doc:\/\/Swidux\/documentation\/Swidux\/PluginFeatureFlagsReference","doc:\/\/Swidux\/documentation\/Swidux\/EntityStoreGuide","doc:\/\/Swidux\/documentation\/Swidux\/PersistenceMiddlewareGuide","doc:\/\/Swidux\/documentation\/Swidux\/KeyValueStoreGuide","doc:\/\/Swidux\/documentation\/Swidux\/GettingStarted","doc:\/\/Swidux\/documentation\/Swidux\/Troubleshooting"],"title":"Reference","generated":true}],"metadata":{"roleHeading":"Article","modules":[{"name":"Swidux"}],"role":"article","title":"Undo \/ Redo"},"variants":[{"traits":[{"interfaceLanguage":"swift"}],"paths":["\/documentation\/swidux\/undoredo"]}],"kind":"article","abstract":[{"type":"text","text":"Add stack-based undo\/redo to your app with "},{"type":"reference","isActive":true,"identifier":"doc:\/\/Swidux\/documentation\/Swidux\/UndoPlugin"},{"type":"text","text":"."}],"hierarchy":{"paths":[["doc:\/\/Swidux\/documentation\/Swidux"]]},"identifier":{"url":"doc:\/\/Swidux\/documentation\/Swidux\/UndoRedo","interfaceLanguage":"swift"},"sections":[],"references":{"doc://Swidux/documentation/Swidux/UndoPlugin":{"identifier":"doc:\/\/Swidux\/documentation\/Swidux\/UndoPlugin","kind":"symbol","role":"symbol","type":"topic","fragments":[{"text":"class","kind":"keyword"},{"text":" ","kind":"text"},{"text":"UndoPlugin","kind":"identifier"}],"title":"UndoPlugin","url":"\/documentation\/swidux\/undoplugin","navigatorTitle":[{"text":"UndoPlugin","kind":"identifier"}],"abstract":[{"text":"Snapshot-based undo\/redo plugin.","type":"text"}]},"doc://Swidux/documentation/Swidux":{"url":"\/documentation\/swidux","kind":"symbol","title":"Swidux","identifier":"doc:\/\/Swidux\/documentation\/Swidux","role":"collection","abstract":[{"text":"Redux-style state management for SwiftUI, with macros for observability and ready-made plugins for persistence, undo, paywalls, version killswitches, and parental gates.","type":"text"}],"type":"topic"},"doc://Swidux/documentation/Swidux/PluginPaywallReference":{"abstract":[{"text":"API reference for the ","type":"text"},{"code":"SwiduxPaywall","type":"codeVoice"},{"text":" library — paywall presentation, entitlement observation, and purchase orchestration.","type":"text"}],"title":"SwiduxPaywall Reference","kind":"article","type":"topic","identifier":"doc:\/\/Swidux\/documentation\/Swidux\/PluginPaywallReference","url":"\/documentation\/swidux\/pluginpaywallreference","role":"article"},"doc://Swidux/documentation/Swidux/GettingStarted":{"abstract":[{"text":"Add Swidux to your project and wire up unidirectional data flow with automatic persistence.","type":"text"}],"title":"Getting Started with Swidux","kind":"article","type":"topic","identifier":"doc:\/\/Swidux\/documentation\/Swidux\/GettingStarted","url":"\/documentation\/swidux\/gettingstarted","role":"article"},"doc://Swidux/documentation/Swidux/EntityStoreGuide":{"abstract":[{"text":"An ordered, keyed collection with built-in change tracking.","type":"text"}],"title":"EntityStore","kind":"article","type":"topic","identifier":"doc:\/\/Swidux\/documentation\/Swidux\/EntityStoreGuide","url":"\/documentation\/swidux\/entitystoreguide","role":"article"},"doc://Swidux/documentation/Swidux/PluginFeatureFlagsReference":{"abstract":[{"text":"API reference for the ","type":"text"},{"code":"SwiduxFeatureFlags","type":"codeVoice"},{"text":" library — typed feature flags, A\/B variants, and remote-tunable scalar values backed by a Swidux-defined JSON wire format.","type":"text"}],"title":"SwiduxFeatureFlags Reference","kind":"article","type":"topic","identifier":"doc:\/\/Swidux\/documentation\/Swidux\/PluginFeatureFlagsReference","url":"\/documentation\/swidux\/pluginfeatureflagsreference","role":"article"},"doc://Swidux/documentation/Swidux/PluginParentalGateReference":{"identifier":"doc:\/\/Swidux\/documentation\/Swidux\/PluginParentalGateReference","url":"\/documentation\/swidux\/pluginparentalgatereference","title":"SwiduxParentalGate Reference","kind":"article","role":"article","abstract":[{"text":"API surface for the ","type":"text"},{"code":"SwiduxParentalGate","type":"codeVoice"},{"text":" library — a domain plugin that guards actions behind a math challenge.","type":"text"}],"type":"topic"},"doc://Swidux/documentation/Swidux/Troubleshooting":{"abstract":[{"text":"Symptoms you may hit while adopting Swidux, and what each one actually means.","type":"text"}],"title":"Troubleshooting","kind":"article","type":"topic","identifier":"doc:\/\/Swidux\/documentation\/Swidux\/Troubleshooting","url":"\/documentation\/swidux\/troubleshooting","role":"article"},"doc://Swidux/documentation/Swidux/MacrosReference":{"kind":"article","title":"Macros","abstract":[{"text":"Reference for ","type":"text"},{"type":"codeVoice","code":"@Swidux"},{"text":" and ","type":"text"},{"type":"codeVoice","code":"@Slice"},{"text":" (the observation bridge between value-type state and SwiftUI), and for ","type":"text"},{"type":"codeVoice","code":"@Persisted"},{"text":" and its property markers (the SwiftData persistence bridge, shipped in ","type":"text"},{"type":"codeVoice","code":"SwiduxPersistence"},{"text":").","type":"text"}],"type":"topic","identifier":"doc:\/\/Swidux\/documentation\/Swidux\/MacrosReference","url":"\/documentation\/swidux\/macrosreference","role":"article"},"doc://Swidux/documentation/Swidux/Store":{"abstract":[{"text":"Generic store that owns the dispatch cycle, plugin lifecycle, and","type":"text"},{"text":" ","type":"text"},{"text":"observation layer.","type":"text"}],"type":"topic","title":"Store","url":"\/documentation\/swidux\/store","identifier":"doc:\/\/Swidux\/documentation\/Swidux\/Store","kind":"symbol","fragments":[{"text":"class","kind":"keyword"},{"text":" ","kind":"text"},{"text":"Store","kind":"identifier"}],"navigatorTitle":[{"text":"Store","kind":"identifier"}],"role":"symbol"},"doc://Swidux/documentation/Swidux/KeyValueStoreGuide":{"abstract":[{"text":"Persist scalar preferences like theme, sort order, or last-seen version — testably, with type-safe keys.","type":"text"}],"title":"KeyValueStore","kind":"article","type":"topic","identifier":"doc:\/\/Swidux\/documentation\/Swidux\/KeyValueStoreGuide","url":"\/documentation\/swidux\/keyvaluestoreguide","role":"collectionGroup"},"doc://Swidux/documentation/Swidux/EntityStore":{"identifier":"doc:\/\/Swidux\/documentation\/Swidux\/EntityStore","title":"EntityStore","role":"symbol","fragments":[{"text":"struct","kind":"keyword"},{"text":" ","kind":"text"},{"text":"EntityStore","kind":"identifier"}],"url":"\/documentation\/swidux\/entitystore","type":"topic","abstract":[{"text":"An ordered, keyed collection of identifiable entities that silently records","type":"text"},{"text":" ","type":"text"},{"text":"every mutation for downstream persistence.","type":"text"}],"navigatorTitle":[{"text":"EntityStore","kind":"identifier"}],"kind":"symbol"},"doc://Swidux/documentation/Swidux/PluginHost":{"identifier":"doc:\/\/Swidux\/documentation\/Swidux\/PluginHost","kind":"symbol","role":"symbol","type":"topic","fragments":[{"text":"class","kind":"keyword"},{"text":" ","kind":"text"},{"text":"PluginHost","kind":"identifier"}],"url":"\/documentation\/swidux\/pluginhost","title":"PluginHost","navigatorTitle":[{"text":"PluginHost","kind":"identifier"}],"abstract":[{"text":"Ordered registry of plugins that drives the dispatch lifecycle.","type":"text"}]},"doc://Swidux/documentation/Swidux/PluginKillswitchReference":{"abstract":[{"text":"Public API surface for the ","type":"text"},{"code":"SwiduxKillswitch","type":"codeVoice"},{"text":" library — the plugin, its state and actions, the service abstraction, and the version-comparison primitives.","type":"text"}],"title":"SwiduxKillswitch Reference","kind":"article","type":"topic","identifier":"doc:\/\/Swidux\/documentation\/Swidux\/PluginKillswitchReference","url":"\/documentation\/swidux\/pluginkillswitchreference","role":"article"},"doc://Swidux/documentation/Swidux/PersistenceMiddlewareGuide":{"title":"Persistence Middleware","abstract":[{"type":"text","text":"Configure automatic persistence that drains entity changes and batches database writes."}],"identifier":"doc:\/\/Swidux\/documentation\/Swidux\/PersistenceMiddlewareGuide","url":"\/documentation\/swidux\/persistencemiddlewareguide","role":"article","type":"topic","kind":"article"},"doc://Swidux/documentation/Swidux/PluginAnalyticsReference":{"abstract":[{"text":"API reference for the ","type":"text"},{"code":"SwiduxAnalytics","type":"codeVoice"},{"text":" library — provider-agnostic analytics with declarative event mapping, auto-identify, and explicit dispatch for the cases the mapper can’t cover.","type":"text"}],"title":"SwiduxAnalytics Reference","kind":"article","type":"topic","identifier":"doc:\/\/Swidux\/documentation\/Swidux\/PluginAnalyticsReference","url":"\/documentation\/swidux\/pluginanalyticsreference","role":"article"}}}